<title>UK: British EU parliament by-election set for Dec 12.</title>
<headline>British EU parliament by-election set for Dec 12.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Voters will choose a new member of the European Parliament in a by-election in Britain's Merseyside West constituency on December 12, the Home Office announced on Thursday.</p>
<p>The poll has been made necessary by the death in September of Kenneth Stewart, the Labour member who won a majority of 51,811 over the Conservatives in the 1994 European elections. -- London Newsroom +44 171 5427767</p>
</text>
